<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.9.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01401</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.9.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b2a22d14-a3ef-4045-888e-4c81508b877f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> The number of people with the flu during an epidemic is a function, \(f\), of the number of days, \(d\), since the epidemic began. The equation \(f(d)=50 \cdot (\frac{3}{2})^d\) defines \(f\).
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item> How many people had the flu at the beginning of the epidemic? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer. </item>
    </list>
  </item>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>50 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> What does \(f(1)\) mean in this situation?  </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>The number of people infected 1 day after the epidemic began. </para>
<blockquote>
  <para>2. The function, \(f\)<emphasis>,</emphasis> gives the dollar value of a bond \(t\) years after the bond was purchased. The graph of \(f\) is shown.</para>
</blockquote>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph of function."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2269474d29cf53c5577e273f7d4b2c88beabe604"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> What is \(f(0)\)? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1000 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> When is \(f(t)=1500\)? Estimate the nearest whole number. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 8 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>A function \(f\) gives the number of stray cats in a town \(t\) years since the town started an animal control program. The program includes both sterilizing stray cats and finding homes to adopt them. An equation representing \(f\) is \(f(t)=243(\frac{1}{3})^t\). </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> What is the value of \(f(t)\) when \(t\) is 0? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 243 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> What is the value of \(f(t)\) when \(t\) is 1? </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 81 </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Function \(g\) gives the amount of a chemical in a person’s body, in milligrams, \(t\) hours since the patient took the drug. The equation \(g(t)=600 \cdot (\frac{3}{5})^t\) defines this function. </item>
</list>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Which is the best choice for the domain of \(g\)?
        </item></list>
<list>
        <item> \(t \geq 0\) </item>
        <item> \(t \geq 600\) </item>
        <item> \(t \leq 600\) </item>
        <item> \(0 \leq t \leq 600\) </item>
      </list>
    

<para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>a. \(t \geq 0\) </para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>Which is the best choice for the range of \(g\)?
        </item></list>
      <list>
        <item> \(g&gt;0\) </item>
        <item> \(g \geq 600\) </item>
        <item> \(g \leq 600\) </item>
        <item> \(0&lt;g \leq 600\) </item>
      </list>
    

<para> <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> d.  \(0&lt;g \leq 600\) </para></section>
</content>
